# ACID -- family: INTERACTION.
# Idea: one macro changes what another means. OPEN is the 303 filter (cutoff
# and resonance in one move, the owner's pairing); BITE is distortion and fold
# while OPEN is low, and turns into resonant squeal and envelope snap as OPEN
# rises (its targets are scaled "by OPEN" in opposite directions).
# Feel if it works: BITE is one "make it nastier" move whose flavour you choose
# with the other hand: tilt shut and it growls, tilt open and it screams.
# Try: OPEN and BITE on the pad, slow line with slides; then WOBL for the
# bass-house wobble, SLIDE for the 303 performance (longer glides, harder
# accents).
# Slow sweeps: OPEN is the set most likely to be swept slowly; near the
# resonance peak (OPEN 0.4..0.7) each 7-bit cutoff step is ~0.7 semitone and
# may be heard as a staircase today (docs/MACROLAB.md, "What a moving
# parameter sounds like"). Judge the sound, not the stepping.
voice bass
name ACID
about "The 303 squelch. Open it, then bite."
base wave=0 sub=34 envmod=70 decay=44 accent=96 fmix=0 lfoshape=sine slide=60 ktrk=40

macro OPEN 0.4
  cutoff   0:16 0.5:60 1:104 smooth
  reso     0:70 0.6:110 1:98           # peaks at 60 % and backs off: squelch, not whistle
  envmod   add 0:12 1:-22              # less envelope once the filter is open by itself
  lvl      0:100 0.6:96 1:98           # the squelch peak is a little hot

macro BITE
  drive    0:22 1:100
  drive    add 0:0 1:-62 by OPEN       # open: BITE drives much less ...
  fold     0:0 1:70
  fold     add 0:0 1:-70 by OPEN       # ... and does not fold at all
  reso     add 0:0 1:16 by OPEN        # ... it squeals instead (edge of self-oscillation)
  envmod   add 0:0 1:28 by OPEN        # ... and snaps harder
  sub      mul 0:1 1:0.55              # thin the sub so the grit reads
  lvl      add 0:0 1:-6 by OPEN        # the squeal is louder than the growl

macro WOBL
  lfodepth 0:0 1:64
  rate     0:1/4 0.35:1/8 0.7:1/8t 0.9:1/16   # an enum: stepped
  cutoff   add 0:0 1:-14               # the LFO only opens: make room under it

macro SLIDE
  slide    0:30 1:110
  accent   0:60 1:127
  decay    add 0:-12 1:24
  adcy     0:80 1:110
